# x3_low_cpu_mem_load: checkpoint not materialised twice. Row four of the per-layer arm.
#
# object     p_census_peak_x2 (97.5% of x2's peak): 866.5 MB float32 weights in pairs (49 flat vs 49
#            shaped, 1 vs 1): from_pretrained holds state_dict and module at once. Markers:
#              after_init                 249,388 kB
#              after_model_load         1,150,172        <- the peak, 0.1 s later
#              after_extract_submodules   384,688        after the layers go to disk
#            arm's peak = checkpoint load (all other levers act later).
# lever      low_cpu_mem_usage=True (meta device, filled tensor by tensor); load high-water ~900 -> 21 MB
#            measured in the image.
# check      mmap'd safetensors may turn anonymous bytes file-backed (file: excluded from W); peak drop
#            matched by a file: row increase = bookkeeping, not a step.
# gate       identical to x2's expected (loading path changes, values do not; fork_rng in place).
# expected   1,135,384 kB -> 450 to 800 MB (-30% to -60%); x2 spread 11%.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_disk_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu,low_cpu_mem_load_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
